  "description": "The Yoji 14” is designed and built specifically for kids 2-4 years old. It is a lightweight (just over 13 lbs) first pedal bike with real off-road capability. The Yoji’s lightweight frame is constructed of formed 6061-T6 aluminum while a newly slimmed-down 4130 Chromoly fork handles the steering. Tektro Mini V-brakes with miniature levers for little hands and the super-soft Brood Tenderiderz grips adorn the 19mm diameter alloy bars. A forged short-reach stem can be flipped to raise the handlebar height in increments. The stem and multiple headset spacers allow parents to adjust the cockpit as kids grow. The Perch mini Pivotal saddle from Brood Bike Co. along with an alloy post make for an ultra-low minimum seat height. The Yoji features sealed cartridge bearings everywhere and 89mm 3-piece alloy cranks designed in-house specifically for little kids. A real cassette hub with a Shimano-compatible cog is a huge upgrade from the coaster brake commonly found on kids' bikes. Topping things off are easily the best off-road tires available in this size - the exclusive 14” x 1.90” Spawn Cycles Loam Star tires with puncture protection.",
